><surname>Blaise</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Bugalho</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Van Lerberghe</surname><given-names>WV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pilfering for survival: how health workers use access to drugs as a coping strategy</article-title><source>Human Resources for Health</source><year>2004</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15059284</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1478-4491-2-1</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Geest</surname><given-names>SV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Self-care and the informal sale of drugs in South Cameroon</article-title><source>Social Science &#x00026; Medicine</source><year>1987</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>293</fpage><lpage>305</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3629303</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0277-9536(87)90232-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Quick</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Hogerzeil</surname><given-names>HV</given-names></name><name><surname>Velasquez</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Rago</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Twenty-five years of essential medicines</article-title><source>Bulletin of the WHO</source><year>2005</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>913</fpage><lpage>914</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Uzochukwu</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Onwujekwe</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Healthcare reform involving the introduction of the user fees and drug revolving funds: influence on health wor